!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-mark-before-the-kernels-record-form-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §12.1"
  description: """
    A definition mark is sugar for a record definition's `extension`, and `!meta.record { … }` is the record that
    sugar lowers to, so the grammar has no mark before it: §12.1 admits `abstract` and `final` before a record body,
    a composition or a subtraction alone. Before `!` the mark is a parse error, wherever the payload states
    `extension` and wherever it does not. The kernel's form states the fact itself, `!meta.record { fields: { … }
    extension: ABSTRACT }`, and the source form is `pet => abstract { name: text }`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
